{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794444964,"nonce":"ZmGn+cq5DZ8yvBce0GMH/z5YhrY=","message":"Committed as ab8d982, not pushed.\n\nThe first open point, decided with the user on 2026-11-12: hxn offers the exit.\n\n`hxn.Loop.exit(code)` is what the fixture's `Finish.exit` was: on hxcpp, outside Emscripten, it flushes standard output and error and calls `_Exit`, declared as an extern on `Loop`; everywhere else it calls `Sys.exit`. A CPPIA script that calls it runs the host's compiled `Loop`, so it gets the same exit. The fixture's two programs end with it and `Finish.hx` is gone.\n\nIt is a way round, for programs that use hxn, and changes nothing in hxcpp: a program that calls `Sys.exit`, or returns from `main`, right after a collection can still crash on Windows. `docs/design.md` gives the reason under Collection, and the conventions have test programs end with it.\n\nStill open: reporting it to hxcpp.\n\nRun: tests/counter/run.sh in cpp, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, hl and gen-hl (Ash in three modes, stock HashLink on the NUC), gen-wasm, gen-emcc and emcc; tests/cli/run.sh on Ash and hxcpp. Not run: Windows, where the crash was, which CI does on push.","files":null}]}